According to the provided context, 'validation data' means data used for providing an evaluation of the trained AI system and for tuning its non-learnable parameters and its learning process in order, inter alia, to prevent underfitting or overfitting. 

Regarding the quality criteria for high-risk AI systems, the context states that training, validation, and testing data sets must "meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2 to 5" and be "subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system," which concern in particular:
(a) the relevant design choices; 
(b) data collection processes and the origin of data, and in the case of personal data, the original purpose of the data collection; 
(c) relevant data-preparation processing operations, such as annotation, labelling, cleaning, updating, enrichment and aggregation; 
(d) the formulation of assumptions, in particular with respect to the information that the data are supposed to measure and represent; and 
(e) an assessment of the availability, quantity and suitability of the data.
